# Line endings for files that are consumed by Linux, regardless of who checked them out.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text
# files to CRLF on checkout. That is harmless for Python and JS — and fatal for a shell
# script that Linux has to execute.
#
# infra/reranker/user_data.sh is the sharp edge. Terraform reads it verbatim via
# templatefile() and hands the result to EC2 as user_data; a CRLF checkout makes the
# shebang "#!/bin/bash\r", cloud-init fails with "bad interpreter", and the instance boots
# with no reranker on it and nothing obvious in the console to say why.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
